course: dictionary
lesson: 6924
title: Words that name a person or a thing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words ending in -er name the person or thing that does an action. A baker bakes, and a swimmer swims. A packer is a person or machine that packs goods into boxes or containers.
explain: Use the words around packer to check its meaning. «Automation is machines doing work people did; one robot replacing 10 packers takes jobs.» The clue is replacing: a robot takes the place of a packer, so a packer is a worker, or a machine, whose job is packing things.
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Packers can also be a name. «Green Bay Packers» is an American football team, and the capital letters show it is a special name, not a job. Look at the capital letters and the words next to the word before you decide.
explain: Swap your meaning into the sentence to test it. «New machines can replace some jobs, like one robot doing the work of 10 packers.» If we put in "one robot doing the work of 10 people who pack goods into boxes", it still makes sense, so the meaning fits.
fact: A packer is a person or machine that packs goods into boxes or containers.
fact: The -er ending often means someone or something that does the action, so a packer packs.
fact: Packers can also be a name: the Green Bay Packers are an American football team.
fact: A capital letter at the start of a name, like Green Bay Packers, tells you it is a special name.
fact: Packers work in places like warehouses, food factories and removal companies.
exercise: «One robot can do the work of 10 packers.» What is a packer? | A football player who wears a helmet | A tool that washes dishes | *A person or machine that packs goods into boxes | A robot that makes boxes out of wood
exercise: Jayden sees «Green Bay Packers» on a sign. What kind of word is Packers here? | A job title for a worker in a warehouse | *The name of an American football team | A type of cardboard box | A machine for sealing tape
exercise: «The packer seals each box with tape.» Copy the word that means the person who packs. | seals | tape | *packer | box
test: The factory needs more packers this week. Who are packers? | *People or machines that pack goods into boxes | People who drive lorries to the shops | Trees that grow in warehouses | Robots that paint walls
test: Why is «Green Bay Packers» written with capital letters? | Because it starts a sentence | Because it is a job title | Because it is very important | *Because it is a special name, the name of a team
exam: «Automation is machines doing work people did; one robot replacing 10 packers takes jobs, but new jobs appear too.» In this sentence, what do packers most likely mean? | Football players who wear pads and helmets | *Workers or machines whose job is packing goods into boxes | Boxes that are full of toys | Robots that build houses
